# Local (private, per-machine) instructions — NOT checked in

`CLAUDE.local.md` is gitignored. Copy this file to `CLAUDE.local.md` and edit the paths.

Keep it to things that are true of **your machine**, not of the codebase — repo facts belong in the
checked-in `CLAUDE.md`, and longer procedures belong in a skill under ``.claude/skills/``.

```markdown
# Local instructions — finetuning-scheduler

## GPU lease (shared multi-GPU host)

This host's GPUs are shared with `interpretune` and the self-hosted Azure agent, and several Claude sessions
may run concurrently, so **serialize all local GPU work**:

    export GPU_LEASE_CMD=~/repos/distributed-insight/project_admin/shared_admin_scripts/gpu_lease.sh

`tests/special_tests.sh` and ``scripts/gen_fts_coverage.sh`` then self re-exec under it. Wrap anything else
GPU-touching explicitly: `$GPU_LEASE_CMD -- <cmd>` (add `--cpu-heavy` for profiling/benchmarks).

- **Expect to wait** (a CI job is ~37 min). Check `$GPU_LEASE_CMD --status` before promising a GPU run;
  do non-GPU work while queued.
- **Notebooks are not lease-aware.** For a long notebook session, reserve deliberately:
  `$GPU_LEASE_CMD --hold --pidfile ~/.gpu_notebook.pid --project notebook-<topic>` and
  `--release` when done. Releasing matters — an unreleased hold blocks CI.
- **Recovery / unexpected holders: use the `gpu-lease` skill.** Never force-reset a CI-held lease
  (`[container]`, `project=azure-<buildId>`); cancel the pipeline run instead.

## Anything else machine-specific

Venv locations, credential-store lookups, private admin-doc paths, etc.
```
